body:
Another possibility I had in mind was to allow both a string (that would be internally converted to a vector) and a list, but that requires a new implementation of `ModuleConfig` (e.g. `ModuleConfig` for an enum `VectorOrString`, or `ModuleConfig` for a new type `VecOrString<'a>(Vec<&'a str>)` that can handle both strings and lists in TOML).

Something like

```rust
pub type VecOrString<'a>(Vec<&'a str>);

impl<'a> ModuleConfig<'a> for VecOrString<'a> {
    fn from_config(config: &'a Value) -> Option<Self> {
        if let Some(string) = config.as_str() {
            return Some(vec![string])
        }

        config
            .as_array()?
            .iter()
            .map(|value| ModuleConfig::from_config(value))
            .collect()
    }
}

```

